\begin_layout Plain Layout

\backslash
ref{tab:ols_learning}
\end_layout

\end_inset

 allows the coefficients to vary across occupational groups.
 In the analysis,
 we will compare coefficient magnitudes and statistical significance across cohorts,
 distinguish the schooling and ability gradients at zero experience and tenure from their subsequent changes.
 Linear combination tests assess whether these gradients change during continued employment with the same employer,
 while joint Wald tests assess whether the corresponding coefficients differ across occupations.
 We then compare the findings with the employer learning evidence of 
